WEBVTT

00:00.890 --> 00:03.690
9,999,994.

00:03.690 --> 00:06.470
Seiya, the gate's about to open.

00:04.420 --> 00:07.250
9,999,995...

00:06.470 --> 00:08.860
We can finally go home!

00:08.860 --> 00:10.740
Wait. I'm still getting ready.

00:12.150 --> 00:13.490
What are you saying?

00:13.490 --> 00:15.890
Don't you want to go home?

00:15.890 --> 00:19.710
I'm more concerned with whether 
that gate is truly safe.

00:19.710 --> 00:21.390
It'll be fine, I bet.

00:21.390 --> 00:24.590
But really, what is this place?

00:24.590 --> 00:29.090
I've never seen a world where the salvation 
difficulty fluctuations between A and SSS.

00:31.980 --> 00:34.580
Can this world be saved?

00:35.060 --> 00:36.060
It'll be fine.

00:36.790 --> 00:40.770
You're incredibly cautious! You 
almost never say things like that!

00:41.120 --> 00:43.180
Do you have a fever?
Let me feel your forehead.

00:43.180 --> 00:43.940
Knock it off.

00:44.610 --> 00:47.250
I already know how to save this world.

00:47.250 --> 00:48.580
You do?

00:49.150 --> 00:52.630
And we're not the one's who can do it.

00:53.050 --> 00:54.890
How can you be so sure?

00:54.890 --> 00:56.090
I've done my research.

00:56.090 --> 00:58.250
When? When did you do that?

00:58.250 --> 00:59.900
While I was asleep?

00:59.900 --> 01:01.070
Now, let's go.

00:59.900 --> 01:01.690
That's scary!

01:01.220 --> 01:03.690
The safest time to jump through 
is 15 seconds from now.

01:03.690 --> 01:05.920
Wait! What does that mean?

01:05.920 --> 01:08.300
Ready... perfectly.

01:08.300 --> 01:08.960
He said the line!

01:09.180 --> 01:10.330
Wait! Hey!

01:10.330 --> 01:12.510
Really, wait!

01:15.210 --> 01:19.470
What's most important here is 
to make the world fun, huh?

01:25.200 --> 01:32.820
ISEKAI QUARTET 3

02:46.580 --> 02:50.020
ISEKAI QUARTET 3

02:50.020 --> 02:52.100
#01: COME TOGETHER! SCHOOL LIFE

02:51.210 --> 02:53.810
And so as you can see,

02:52.100 --> 02:53.810
CLASS 2

02:53.810 --> 02:59.770
this semester will be full 
of events, so have fun!

02:59.770 --> 03:02.850
Sir, I demand another seat change!

03:01.050 --> 03:05.780
Now, let's wrap up our homeroom.

03:07.530 --> 03:09.660
And so Richo became a tiger...

03:10.830 --> 03:12.150
Otto.

03:12.150 --> 03:14.560
It's kind of rude to interrupt...

03:14.560 --> 03:16.940
Well I'm used to people like that.

03:16.940 --> 03:18.010
What is it?

03:18.010 --> 03:22.750
I heard from Subaru that you 
can hear the voices of animals.

03:22.750 --> 03:25.290
Yes, it's called the Soul of Language.

03:25.290 --> 03:28.310
I can understand what most living things say.

03:28.310 --> 03:31.390
Great. You can be in charge of the animals then?

03:31.390 --> 03:35.660
The animals? I think Natsuki-san does that too.

03:36.110 --> 03:39.530
But if I do it, wouldn't there 
be nothing for Natsuki-san to do?

03:39.530 --> 03:41.310
Hey!

03:41.310 --> 03:42.680
Don't underestimate me!

03:42.680 --> 03:43.030
I'm...

03:43.030 --> 03:45.780
Hamsuke's favorite food, after all!

03:45.780 --> 03:47.700
Yes, I'm his favorite food...

03:47.700 --> 03:48.520
Aura!

03:48.520 --> 03:49.390
Am I wrong?

03:49.390 --> 03:51.240
Then Death Knight's toy?

03:51.240 --> 03:56.160
Don't worry, Subaru! I'm a goddess, and 
I will happily solve your undead problems!

03:56.160 --> 03:59.880
That foolish self-proclaimed goddess 
is getting a big head again.

04:00.150 --> 04:02.330
Did you say something?

04:02.760 --> 04:05.340
I said you're a fool.

04:06.100 --> 04:09.940
On the last test, I, of 
course, got a perfect score.

04:09.940 --> 04:12.420
What did you get?

04:12.420 --> 04:13.670
Twelve percent.

04:14.450 --> 04:15.500
Kazuma!

04:15.500 --> 04:16.180
Yup, I'm Kazuma.

04:16.180 --> 04:17.480
Why did you tell her?

04:17.480 --> 04:20.290
To get so angry when
the truth is revealed...

04:20.290 --> 04:22.090
You really are a fool.

04:23.990 --> 04:27.370
I-I got a below average score!

04:28.010 --> 04:30.790
There are just too many people 
with good grades in this class!

04:30.790 --> 04:33.900
You did great, Shalltear-san!

04:33.900 --> 04:36.130
I'm doing my best! I mean it!

04:34.900 --> 04:38.060
Should I say something?

04:36.130 --> 04:38.060
I know! I know!

04:38.060 --> 04:40.490
I think you can ignore them.

04:40.490 --> 04:42.310
It's nothing new.

04:42.630 --> 04:47.290
Yes. Rerugen-sensei is about to get mad.

04:47.290 --> 04:51.030
Do you think you could quiet down?

04:47.570 --> 04:51.990
ENSAN RICHO

04:55.460 --> 04:58.660
So... Garfiel and Otto, was it?

04:59.110 --> 05:01.830
You're Subaru's buddies, right?

05:01.830 --> 05:04.050
It feels embarrassing to say it...

05:04.050 --> 05:05.550
Yes. We're friends.

05:05.550 --> 05:07.770
You really are always...

05:07.770 --> 05:10.160
Is there a problem?

05:10.160 --> 05:15.130
What, are you embarrassed we're 
saying we're your buds, Boss?

05:15.130 --> 05:16.410
Boss?

05:16.410 --> 05:18.140
That's what I call him.

05:18.140 --> 05:20.920
I never call him anything else.

05:21.470 --> 05:24.530
Subaru, are you actually a boss?

05:24.530 --> 05:31.020
No, I'm nobody special. It's all I can do to 
keep up with the incredible people around me.

05:31.020 --> 05:33.050
Indeed, indeed...

05:33.050 --> 05:35.140
No, look...

05:35.140 --> 05:37.390
Hey, Darkness!

05:37.390 --> 05:38.210
Kazuma!

05:38.210 --> 05:40.450
Why are you guys all standing around Weiss?

05:40.940 --> 05:46.070
We were talking about how Weiss 
might actually be really strong.

05:46.070 --> 05:50.080
So we decided to measure how strong.

05:50.080 --> 05:53.910
No, I'm not as strong as you guys think.

05:53.910 --> 05:55.730
You're so humble.

05:55.730 --> 05:57.880
You're actually quite strong.

05:57.880 --> 05:58.660
Yup.

05:58.660 --> 05:59.300
Indeed!

05:59.300 --> 06:00.930
You guys...

06:01.270 --> 06:03.840
So, how are you going to measure it?

06:03.840 --> 06:08.600
I've heard sumo is the best 
way to measure strength.

06:08.600 --> 06:11.840
Sumo? Whose idea is that? Darkness?

06:11.840 --> 06:13.510
Why do you think it's me?

06:13.510 --> 06:15.900
You seem you'd like sumo.

06:15.900 --> 06:17.330
What does that mean?

06:17.330 --> 06:21.410
I've been thinking, you all seem 
to have the wrong idea about me.

06:21.410 --> 06:24.460
I think they understand you 
really well, Lady Lalatina.

06:23.070 --> 06:26.030
Garfiel, you want to play, huh?

06:24.730 --> 06:26.410
Kazuma, I told you, don't call me that!

06:26.410 --> 06:28.380
Why, Lady Lalatina?

06:26.740 --> 06:31.410
I can't go all out against you or the boss.

06:28.380 --> 06:31.410
It's a fine name, Lady Lalatina!

06:31.410 --> 06:34.790
Then let's help out.

06:35.260 --> 06:36.830
LIBRARY

06:38.710 --> 06:40.580
Subaru!

06:41.290 --> 06:43.010
Bea-ko!

06:43.390 --> 06:44.680
You been a good girl?

06:44.680 --> 06:48.050
Beatrice really cheered 
up, huh? All of a sudden.

06:48.050 --> 06:50.100
Y-Yeah.

06:50.100 --> 06:51.980
Really?

06:52.790 --> 06:55.600
She was always like this.

06:55.600 --> 06:56.710
Seriously?

06:56.710 --> 07:00.900
So, Subaru, did you need 
something from me, I wonder?

07:00.900 --> 07:05.030
Well, it's actually not you... Mare!

07:05.030 --> 07:06.900
Can you do me a favor!

07:07.330 --> 07:09.460
M-Me?

07:11.190 --> 07:14.870
Really, sumo is so barbaric.

07:15.950 --> 07:19.930
Well, I assume Albedo will win.

07:19.930 --> 07:25.040
But that... beast-man? Gar-something 
or other? He looks strong too.

07:25.040 --> 07:27.370
What do you think, Rem?

07:27.370 --> 07:30.720
Garf? I don't think he's that strong.

07:30.720 --> 07:32.930
Harsh.

07:32.930 --> 07:34.760
I could be a lot harsher.

07:36.070 --> 07:37.620
Sheesh...

07:38.380 --> 07:40.310
Why am I doing this?

07:40.310 --> 07:44.260
We're the only ones who know 
the rules. What do you want?

07:44.260 --> 07:46.870
Make Kazuma do it.

07:46.870 --> 07:48.100
Hell no.

07:48.100 --> 07:51.140
Getting between any two of those 
idiots is a death sentence.

07:51.140 --> 07:54.380
Wait, are you saying I'm likely to survive it?

07:54.380 --> 07:57.900
Why aren't I getting hazard pay for this?

07:57.900 --> 07:59.180
Give it up.

08:00.540 --> 08:02.880
Naofumi-dono! Can you do me a favor—

08:02.880 --> 08:03.540
I refuse.

08:03.540 --> 08:04.630
That was fast!

08:04.630 --> 08:08.300
Master's making us a cake today!

08:08.790 --> 08:11.720
So yeah... Sorry! Really!

08:11.720 --> 08:13.970
A cake! Aww...

08:13.970 --> 08:15.550
Visha, calm down.

08:16.410 --> 08:18.620
I also want cake!

08:18.620 --> 08:20.940
And you, Weiss, just stand up.

08:21.640 --> 08:26.560
TEACHER'S OFFICE

08:21.640 --> 08:26.560
So, what did you want to talk about?

08:26.560 --> 08:32.330
I wanted to talk about how we suddenly 
found ourselves in another world earlier...

08:32.330 --> 08:35.420
That was certainly a surprise!

08:35.420 --> 08:40.430
I came to the classroom in the 
morning and no one was here!

08:40.430 --> 08:45.610
That was a different kind of teleportation 
than the one that brought us here.

08:46.350 --> 08:47.390
Oh?

08:48.130 --> 08:51.340
Ainz-sama, where are you?

08:51.340 --> 08:53.590
Come watch me win!

08:54.210 --> 08:55.910
The winner is Albedo.

08:55.910 --> 08:59.850
Hmm. so your theory is that in your old world,

08:59.850 --> 09:01.780
Nice, miss.

09:00.180 --> 09:07.980
there exists another version of 
yourself that you are based on?

09:01.780 --> 09:05.420
But your victory streak ends here!

09:07.980 --> 09:11.020
'cause now you must fight me!

09:07.980 --> 09:14.660
Yes. Our thoughts and awareness are 
changing without us being aware of it.

09:11.010 --> 09:15.830
Now, the final battle between 
Albedo and Garfiel will begin!

09:15.830 --> 09:18.280
Yay!

09:18.550 --> 09:22.290
What? If there's something 
you want to say, then say it!

09:21.670 --> 09:25.810
I'm sure this is true for 
the others, as well as me.

09:22.290 --> 09:24.460
I'm saying that you're an idiot.

09:28.110 --> 09:33.180
Our experiences in our original 
world are influencing us somehow.

09:35.290 --> 09:38.370
Even as we speak.

09:39.550 --> 09:40.450
Hmm.

09:41.460 --> 09:47.440
And so I assume that we ourselves 
are copies made from other worlds.

09:47.440 --> 09:51.190
We're fakes, you say?

09:51.190 --> 09:54.950
Not the originals, at least.

09:55.790 --> 09:59.420
An interesting hypothesis!

10:00.210 --> 10:01.660
And so?

10:01.660 --> 10:03.990
What do you want to do?

10:03.990 --> 10:10.050
Despair at the fact that you're a 
fake, and live your life in misery?

10:10.580 --> 10:12.060
Or...

10:12.060 --> 10:13.790
I have a theory.

10:16.050 --> 10:21.740
If our originals are affecting 
us from their worlds,

10:21.740 --> 10:26.890
is it not possible that we 
can affect them as well?

10:26.890 --> 10:30.800
Turn things around, then?

10:30.800 --> 10:33.980
I assume you've had the same thought.

10:36.390 --> 10:37.720
You...

10:37.720 --> 10:40.460
No, not just you.

10:40.460 --> 10:43.690
The students here really are fascinating.

10:44.030 --> 10:47.980
So, what should we do now?

10:47.980 --> 10:51.790
Why are you asking me?

10:51.790 --> 10:55.650
Because you're our teacher.

10:56.130 --> 10:58.530
Roswaal-"sensei".

10:59.880 --> 11:03.980
Indeed. Indeed, that's correct.

11:04.330 --> 11:08.630
Let me give you some advice, as your teacher.

11:09.970 --> 11:15.950
Why don't we all try and be even 
better friends than before!

11:20.330 --> 11:21.330
Ainz!

11:21.330 --> 11:21.890
What is it?

11:21.890 --> 11:25.910
Albedo and the new transfer student, 
Garfiel, are playing sumo,

11:25.910 --> 11:28.580
and they're messing up the yard!

11:28.580 --> 11:30.660
Okay. I don't understand at all.

11:30.660 --> 11:32.210
Just come with us!

11:32.210 --> 11:33.750
Okay! Got it!

11:55.330 --> 11:56.090
Mare!

11:56.090 --> 11:57.310
Can you maintain the base they're standing on?

11:57.310 --> 12:00.490
I'm trying! But I can't keep up!

12:03.450 --> 12:07.700
I didn't expect anybody to 
be able to keep up with me!

12:07.700 --> 12:11.660
I couldn't be the Overseer of the Guardians 
if I'd lose to the likes of you!

12:17.990 --> 12:23.910
'cause even I don't know what's coming next.

12:25.260 --> 12:29.850
Dragon. Goddess. Witch. X.

12:33.770 --> 12:38.130
You won't have your way with this world, too.

12:49.490 --> 12:51.920
Well, no matter what this world is,

12:51.920 --> 12:55.000
I'm just going to do what I want.
